    <string name="settings_section">System</string>
    <string name="eink_info">What each mode does</string>
    <string name="eink_note">How the screen redraws. Faster modes leave more ghosting behind; slower ones are cleaner but blink more.</string>
    <string name="eink_note_fast">Fast, no blink. Very high contrast; crushes dark colours and shadows to black.</string>
    <string name="eink_note_soft">Fast, no blink. Less contrast, so darker colours keep some detail.</string>
    <string name="eink_note_dither">Fast, two inks, dots of grey. Less contrast, and the best way to keep detail at speed.</string>
    <string name="eink_note_text">Sharp greys for reading. Slower to redraw.</string>
    <string name="eink_note_quality">The cleanest picture. Slowest, and it blinks.</string>
    <string name="app_modes_note">Give an app its own e-ink mode. It is applied when the app opens, and the master mode returns when you leave it.</string>
